2026-06-28 - Project bootstrap and specification set
Status: DOCUMENTED
================================================================================

Goal:
Create the specification set and the Make Spec method for the WaveShare
ESP32-S3-ePaper-1.54, using the M5Stack Dial project in Sample/ as the reference
structure. The device was NOT connected during this session.

Findings (DOCUMENTED, from the official product page + datasheets,
review date 2026-06-28):
- MCU: ESP32-S3, dual-core Xtensa LX7 @ 240 MHz; 512 KB SRAM; 384 KB ROM.
- Memory: 8 MB flash and 8 MB PSRAM (stacked).
- Display: 1.54" e-paper, 200 x 200, black/white, microcapsule electrophoretic,
  bistable; full refresh ~2 s, partial refresh ~0.3 s; SPI; ~180 deg viewing.
- Wireless: 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi (802.11 b/g/n); Bluetooth 5 LE; internal antenna.
- Sensors: SHTC3 temperature/humidity; PCF85063 RTC.
- Audio: ES8311 codec, on-board microphone, speaker via MX1.25 2-pin connector.
- Buttons: PWR (customizable) and BOOT (download mode).
- Touch: FT6336 capacitive over I2C — TOUCH VARIANT ONLY.
- Storage: micro-SD (FAT32).
- Expansion: 2 x 6-pin headers (2.54 mm); GPIO, UART, I2C.
- USB: Type-C (ESP32-S3). Power: 3.7 V Li-battery (MX1.25), onboard charge/
  discharge management.
- This board has NO rotary encoder and NO RFID (unlike the M5Stack Dial).
- Exact physical dimensions and the pre-installed factory demo were not captured
  from the product page; confirm from the WaveShare wiki and from the device.

