2026-06-29 - Reference docs recorded; V1 vs V2 memory difference found
Status: DOCUMENTED
================================================================================

Goal:
Record the official documentation/wiki references for this product, and capture
which variant/version distinctions matter (user unsure which unit is in hand).

Primary reference pages (review date 2026-06-29):
- Official docs (covers all four SKUs + V1/V2):
  https://docs.waveshare.net/ESP32-S3-ePaper-1.54/?variant=ESP32-S3-Touch-ePaper-1.54
- Wiki (V2, non-touch):
  https://www.waveshare.net/wiki/ESP32-S3-ePaper-1.54-V2

Findings:
- The product line has FOUR SKUs:
  - ESP32-S3-ePaper-1.54        (non-touch, with battery)
  - ESP32-S3-ePaper-1.54-EN     (non-touch, no battery)
  - ESP32-S3-Touch-ePaper-1.54  (capacitive touch, with battery)
  - ESP32-S3-Touch-ePaper-1.54-EN (capacitive touch, no battery)
- There are TWO hardware versions, distinguishable by PCB markings:
  - V1: 4 MB Flash / 2 MB PSRAM
  - V2: 8 MB Flash / 8 MB PSRAM, improved power efficiency
- CORRECTION to the 2026-06-28 entry: the "8 MB flash + 8 MB PSRAM" figure is
  specific to V2. A V1 unit has 4 MB / 2 MB. Until the device is read, treat
  flash/PSRAM size as version-dependent and confirm with `esptool flash_id`.
- All SKUs share the core architecture: ESP32-S3 LX7 @ 240 MHz, 1.54" 200x200
  e-paper, 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi, BLE 5, ES8311 audio + mic + speaker, SHTC3, PCF85063,
  micro-SD, PWR/BOOT buttons, USB-C, 2x6 expansion headers.
- The wiki/docs link resources to verify later: schematic PDF, Arduino + ESP-IDF
  demo code, datasheets (ESP32-S3, PCF85063, SHTC3, e-paper), and LVGL
  (v8.3.11 / v9.3.0) for the touch variant UI.

Open questions to resolve from the device (still pending USB connection):
- Touch vs non-touch SKU.
- Battery vs -EN (no battery) SKU.
- V1 vs V2 (PCB marking; confirm flash/PSRAM via esptool flash_id).
- Device MAC and factory firmware behavior.

