2026-06-29 - Custom app: ABC touch-toggle e-paper firmware
Status: DEVICE VERIFIED
================================================================================

Goal:
Add an interface: tap the e-paper -> show big "ABC"; tap again -> original page.

Design decisions (evidence-based):
- Framework = Arduino-ESP32 3.x. Reason: WaveShare's FT6336 touch driver uses the
  new driver/i2c_master.h API (ESP-IDF 5.2+). The locally installed ESP-IDF is
  v5.1.3 (too old for that API), and no Arduino core was installed. Arduino-ESP32
  3.x ships the right I2C API and is WaveShare's documented path for this board.
- Reused WaveShare's own, tested board drivers (correct pins guaranteed), copied
  unmodified from github.com/waveshareteam/ESP32-S3-ePaper-1.54 examples
  09_LVGL_V8_Test (epaper_driver_bsp, board_power_bsp) and 12_FT6336_Test
  (ft6336_bsp, i2c_bsp, user_config.h).
- No LVGL/font dependency: embedded a 5x7 font scaled up for big "ABC".
- Full refresh per toggle (clean, ~2 s) instead of partial (avoids ghosting).

Confirmed pin map (from WaveShare user_config.h):
- EPD: DC=10 CS=11 SCK=12 MOSI=13 RST=9 BUSY=8 PWR=6
- I2C: SDA=47 SCL=48 (FT6336 0x38, RTC 0x51, SHTC3 0x70); touch INT=21 RST=7
- Buttons: BOOT=0 PWR=18

Implementation notes (from reading the driver source):
- e-paper buffer is 1bpp, 200x200 = 5000 bytes; pixel index = y*25 + (x>>3),
  bit = 7-(x&7); WHITE sets the bit, BLACK clears it.
- EPD_Clear() memsets buffer to white; EPD_Display() flushes (full refresh).
- Driver allocates its buffer in PSRAM (MALLOC_CAP_SPIRAM) -> the Arduino build
  MUST enable PSRAM (OPI) or it asserts at boot.
- Touch read: ft6336->GetTouchPoint(&x,&y) returns nonzero when touched; the app
  toggles on the rising edge (one tap = one toggle), polled at ~20 Hz.

Files: firmware/ABC_Touch_Toggle/ (ABC_Touch_Toggle.ino + README + copied BSPs).

Build/flash contract (Arduino-ESP32 3.x):
- FQBN: esp32:esp32:esp32s3:PSRAM=opi,FlashSize=8M,USBMode=hwcdc,CDCOnBoot=cdc,
  PartitionScheme=default_8MB
- arduino-cli compile/upload; port /dev/cu.usbmodem* (detect each time).

Status/limitations:
- Recovery: factory image preserved at
  backup/esp32s3-epaper154-full-flash-2026-06-29.bin.

Build/flash results (2026-06-29):
- BUILD VERIFIED: arduino-cli compile OK. Sketch 355268 B (10% of 3.34 MB app
  partition); globals 22956 B (7% RAM). esp32 core 3.3.10, FQBN
  esp32:esp32:esp32s3:PSRAM=opi,FlashSize=8M,USBMode=hwcdc,CDCOnBoot=cdc,
  PartitionScheme=default_8MB.
- FLASH VERIFIED: arduino-cli upload to /dev/cu.usbmodem11201; esptool "Hash of
  data verified", hard reset into the app. This replaced the factory firmware.
- USB port stayed stable across two 120 s monitors -> app is NOT crash-looping
  (a PSRAM/boot crash would re-enumerate repeatedly). PSRAM=opi is correct for
  the N8R8 module (8 MB octal). So the app booted and should display.
- Serial console: no bytes captured over the native USB-Serial/JTAG CDC (even
  after an RTS reset pulse with DTR asserted). Likely an HWCDC capture quirk, not
  an app fault. Device-VISUAL confirmation (screen + tap) still pending the user's
  report; touch SKU still to be confirmed that way.
- TODO if touch is dead on-screen: rebuild with the PWR/BOOT button as the toggle
  input (touch_bsp absent on a non-touch unit would also explain no reaction).

UPDATE (2026-06-29): home screen + ABC (user clarified they wanted the original
display retained, not replaced by a bare page; one firmware runs at a time, so
the "home" display is built into the same app).
- v2 of the app: home screen shows LIVE temperature + humidity (SHTC3 @0x70) and
  time (PCF85063 RTC @0x51, seeded to 12:00 since no NTP), refreshed ~once/min;
  tap -> big ABC; tap -> home. SHTC3/RTC are read directly on the existing
