2026-06-29 - BLE-connected e-paper + iOS companion app
Status: BUILD VERIFIED / FLASH VERIFIED (firmware); iOS code complete (Xcode build by user)
================================================================================

Goal:
iOS app that connects over BLE to (1) read temp/humidity/time, set the clock,
rename the BLE device, view/set Wi-Fi; and (2) upload a photo that replaces the
on-device picture (app converts to the e-paper size/format).

Firmware (firmware/ePaper_BLE/, evolved from ABC_Touch_Toggle):
- Arduino-ESP32 3.x BLEDevice GATT server + WiFi + Preferences(NVS), plus the
  existing e-paper/touch/SHTC3/PCF85063 code.
- Info service f0a00000-...: temp/humidity (read+notify), time (read+write -> sets
  RTC), BLE name (read+write -> persists to NVS and reboots to re-advertise),
  wifi SSID/pass (write, NVS), wifiCtrl (write "scan"/"connect"), wifiStatus
  (read+notify). Wi-Fi scan/connect are DEFERRED to loop() (not run in the BLE
  callback) to avoid blocking the BLE stack.
- Image service f0b00000-...: imgCtrl ("START"/"COMMIT"/"CLEAR"), imgData
  (write-no-response, sequential chunks), imgStat (notify). On COMMIT the 5000-
  byte 1bpp image is stored in NVS and rendered. Format: 200x200, 25 bytes/row,
  MSB=leftmost, bit 1=WHITE 0=BLACK (matches the driver buffer).
- Home screen = temp/humidity/time; tap toggles to the uploaded picture (or "ABC"
  if none). MTU requested 517.
- BUILD VERIFIED: 1175429 B (35% of 3.34 MB app), globals 52300 B (15% RAM).
  FLASH VERIFIED to /dev/cu.usbmodem11201 (hash verified). Advertises 'ePaper-154'.
- Device-level BLE behavior to be confirmed by the user via the app / nRF Connect.

iOS app (ios/ePaperBLE/, SwiftUI + CoreBluetooth, iOS 17+):
- BLEManager (scan/connect/discover/notify/write, paced write-without-response
  chunk upload via canSendWriteWithoutResponse + peripheralIsReadyToSend...).
- ImageConverter (resize to 200x200 aspect-fill, grayscale, Floyd-Steinberg
  dither, pack to the firmware's exact byte layout; live preview).
- InfoTabView, ImageTabView, ePaperBLEApp (TabView). UUIDs match the firmware.
- Build steps + Info.plist (NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription) in ios/README.md.

