================================================================================
2026-06-29 - Battery power-hold required (device died on USB unplug)
Status: ROOT-CAUSED + fix coded (reflash/device-verify pending)
================================================================================

Symptom (user, with a LiPo battery attached to the MX1.25 connector):
- With the factory firmware, the e-paper kept showing its image after USB was
  unplugged. With my custom firmware, unplugging USB made the device go fully
  dead - not even a static e-paper image.

Root cause (high confidence, from reading board_power_bsp.cpp):
- This board uses a battery POWER-HOLD LATCH on VBAT_PWR_PIN = GPIO17.
  VBAT_POWER_ON() drives GPIO17 HIGH = keep the system powered from the battery;
  VBAT_POWER_OFF() drives it LOW = release (power off on battery).
- While USB is connected the board is powered via USB regardless, so the bug is
  invisible on USB. The instant USB is removed, if GPIO17 is not HIGH the battery
  path is not latched -> the whole board loses power immediately. The abrupt cut
  also prevents the e-paper from latching a clean static image (so: no image AND
  no function).
- The factory firmware asserts the power-hold, which is why IT survived unplug.
- My custom firmwares (ABC_Touch_Toggle and ePaper_BLE) called POWEER_EPD_ON()
  but never VBAT_POWER_ON(), so they died on unplug. This is the regression.

Power-pin polarity reference (from board_power_bsp.cpp):
- EPD_PWR (GPIO6):  active-LOW  -> POWEER_EPD_ON() sets it 0
- Audio_PWR (GPIO42): active-LOW -> POWEER_Audio_ON() sets it 0
- VBAT_PWR (GPIO17): active-HIGH -> VBAT_POWER_ON() sets it 1  (battery hold)

Fix:
- Call board_power.VBAT_POWER_ON() as the FIRST line of setup() (before anything
  else) so the board latches battery power immediately at boot. Applied to
  firmware/ePaper_BLE/ePaper_BLE.ino; BUILD VERIFIED (1175453 B). Reflash pending
  the device being reconnected to USB; then verify: unplug USB -> stays running.
- TODO: apply the same one-liner to firmware/ABC_Touch_Toggle/ for parity.

Note on e-paper retention (secondary): the panel is bistable and holds a
FULLY-refreshed image with no power, but cutting power mid-refresh or while the
controller is active can prevent a clean latch. The driver exposes no deep-sleep
(0x10) command. With the power-hold fix the board simply stays powered on
battery, so this is moot for normal use; an explicit EPD deep-sleep remains an
optional robustness improvement if true power-off retention is ever needed.

================================================================================
2026-06-29 - Battery life: always-on firmware drains in hours (DEVICE OBSERVED)
================================================================================

- User running the ePaper_BLE firmware on battery: it drained to 0% within hours
  (e-paper froze on its last frame, e.g. "02:01 BAT 00%", when the chip lost
  power). The home screen now shows battery % (ADC GPIO4) + BT/Wi-Fi status.
- Cause: the firmware is not power-optimized. It never sleeps (loop polls touch
  every 40 ms), and BLE ADVERTISES CONTINUOUSLY even when the screen shows
  "BT:OFF" (that label means "no client connected", not "radio off"). Estimated
  active draw ~40-70 mA on a ~200-500 mAh LiPo => ~3-8 h.
- Low-power path: e-paper holds its image at 0 power, so "draw -> deep sleep ->
  wake on timer/touch/button -> redraw" yields ~10-50 uA sleep => weeks-months.
  Deep sleep and always-advertising BLE are mutually exclusive.
- Action: added a standing rule to the specs (AI/Functional/ClaudeDesign/Make
  Spec) to ASK the user their target battery life and recommend a power mode
  before building battery firmware. Implementing a low-power mode is offered as
  the next step (not yet built; current firmware remains always-on).

================================================================================
2026-06-29 - On-demand BLE (tap to enable, 3-min auto-off)
Status: FLASH VERIFIED (uploaded /dev/cu.usbmodem1101, hash verified)
================================================================================

Change to firmware/ePaper_BLE (per user, to cut the BLE drain):
- BLE no longer advertises continuously. It is OFF by default; a screen TAP calls
  startAdv() (advertise + arm a 3-minute window). If nobody connects within 3 min
  it stops advertising; on disconnect it also stops (no auto-re-advertise). The
  BLE stack stays initialized so re-enabling is instant; "off" = not advertising/
  not discoverable (the main radio drain), not a full controller power-down.
- Tap keeps its existing job (toggle home<->picture) AND now (re)opens the BLE
  window; while connected a tap just toggles the screen.
- Home status row BT field is now 3-state: OFF / ADV (advertising) / ON
  (connected). Added font glyphs D and V for "ADV".
- Everything else unchanged (sensors, time, battery %, Wi-Fi, image upload).
- BUILD VERIFIED (1186365 B, 35%). Reflash pending the device on USB.
- Note: this is NOT deep sleep — the CPU is still always awake; it removes the
  continuous BLE advertising. The full weeks-per-charge design is the separate
  "Idea - periodic update.md" concept.
